      "what": "The researchers developed T-STAR, a two-stage transformer-based framework that forecasts station-level bike-sharing demand at a 15-minute resolution. Tested on Washington D.C.’s Capital Bikeshare system, the model separates coarse hourly patterns from high-frequency fluctuations by integrating real-time metro demand variations and localized inputs to generate probabilistic predictions.",
